+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the providers to shape the call the model produces. This spec makes the registry enforce that same schema where the model's call enters the engine: `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs, so a malformed call becomes a readable tool result the model can correct within the existing tool-round budget instead of an exception that ends the conversation. Validation enforces `required`, declared property types and `enum` only — it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types, or apply defaults, and there is no opt-out flag.
+
+## The validation boundary
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required property before the executor runs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L82)).
+- A call the schema rejects returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure, rather than throwing ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required property before the executor runs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L82)).
+- The executor is never invoked for a rejected call ([validated by: names the property path and expected type when a field has the wrong type, without echoing the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+- A rejection names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and never contains a property value ([validated by: names the property path and expected type when a field has the wrong type, without echoing the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+- No log line written for a rejected call contains a property value ([validated by: never echoes a rejected payload value into the result or the logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L232)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor unchanged, exactly once per call: no injected defaults, no coercion, and unlisted extra properties pass through ([validated by: passes valid input with an unlisted extra property through to the executor unchanged, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L115)).
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time, so an uncompilable schema throws at registration with a message naming the tool, and nothing is registered for it ([validated by: compiles the schema at register time, throwing a message that names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L128)).
+- A static tool's schema stays in force across repeated `execute` calls ([validated by: holds the registered schema in force across ten execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L176)).
+- A schema produced by a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves and compiles per call, cached by the resolved schema object, so a definition whose schema differs between calls is validated against the schema current at that call, not a stale cached one ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L147)).
+
+## Conversation flow
+
+- A rejected call is fed back to the model as a tool result, so the tool loop continues and a corrected retry can succeed within the same message ([validated by: returns the rejection to the model so a corrected retry continues the conversation](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L195)).
+- The tool-round bound (`DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS = 5`) is what stops a rejection-and-retry cycle from spinning: each rejected call costs a round, so a model that never corrects its call is stopped by the existing round budget rather than by validation.
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name, unchanged ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L226)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Validating tool _output_, hallucination detection, and an evaluation harness.
+- Per-tool authorization: a schema-valid call for someone else's data is still valid, and authorization is a separate `ToolContext` boundary concern — _Let a consumer decline a tool call through a `beforeToolCall` hook_ is a veto seam, not an authorization model.
+- Retry, timeout and rate limiting around tool execution, and any actual tool implementation, which is written against this contract later.
+- Returning an unknown tool name to the model instead of throwing: the `Unknown tool: <name>` throw stays as-is and is tracked separately.
+
+## Packaging
+
+- The validator is a runtime dependency of the package, not a peer or dev dependency, and the compiled package still imports cleanly.
